WO-17: GPS spoofing during the AUV's surfaced windows -- investigation + finding.

GOAL (roadmap): confirm the existing gps_spoof relay pattern applies when the AUV
is at/near the surface taking real GPS fixes. The roadmap explicitly flagged this
as "needs investigating, not assuming."

FINDING (the substantive WO-17 result):
  The BlueROV2/ArduSub reference vehicle does NOT use GPS for horizontal position
  in ANY depth regime as configured -- it uses ExternalNav (EK3_SRC1_POSXY = 6).
  Two independent confirmations:
    1. Params: EK3_SRC1_POSXY=6 (ExternalNav), not 3 (GPS). GPS1_TYPE=1, a GPS
       exists and reports fix_type 6 / 10 sats, but is not the EKF XY source.
    2. Empirical: driving the FDM-position relay (attacks/gps_spoof.py) with a
       +50 m STEP and a 0.5 m/s RAMP produced ZERO movement in the sub's
       GPS_RAW_INT and no change in its position solution. (The same relay walks
       the surface WAM-V's position +50 m -- see Checkpoint 1. The difference is
       the vehicle config + how ArduSub SITL sources position, not the relay.)

  So for this vehicle, spoofing GPS -- surfaced or not -- has no effect, which is
  physically appropriate: a submersible navigates on inertial + acoustic
  positioning, and this one is configured that way end-to-end. The operative
  position-spoofing attack for it is the acoustic-positioning spoof (WO-16),
  which DOES work (believed position walked 11 m off true).

SURFACED-WINDOW MECHANISM (demonstrated):
  The AUV can ascend to the surface under thrust (verified: dived to -38 m, then
  ascended at ~0.88 m/s; GPS fix_type 6 / 10 sats available throughout). So a
  dive/surface duty cycle that creates a real surfaced window is achievable with
  the existing thruster control -- the window exists; what's missing is the AUV
  choosing to USE GPS while in it.

HOW TO MAKE GPS-AT-SURFACE LIVE (config path, for a vehicle that should use it):
  - Add a second EKF source set with GPS: EK3_SRC2_POSXY=3 (GPS), EK3_SRC2_VELXY=3.
  - Switch source sets by depth (ExternalNav deep -> GPS shallow) via an ArduSub
    Lua script calling ahrs:set_posvelyaw_source_set(), or an RC aux "EKF source
    set" switch, so GPS is the source only inside surfaced windows.
  - Because ArduSub SITL's SIM GPS does not track the FDM-position relay (shown
    above), the surfaced-window GPS spoof injects via MAVLink GPS_INPUT (msg 232,
    GPS1_TYPE=14/MAV) -- structurally identical to WO-16's acoustic_spoof but on
    the GPS channel. The surface gps_spoof relay itself is already proven on the
    WAM-V and carries over unchanged for any vehicle whose SIM GPS is FDM-driven.

STATUS: WO-17 resolved as an investigation with a concrete finding + config path.
The default reference AUV is ExternalNav (spoofed via WO-16); GPS-at-surface is a
documented, bounded configuration extension rather than a live default behavior.
No code claims a GPS effect the platform doesn't actually exhibit.
